rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates separation of concerns between Runner (orchestration), Workflows
    (reasoning), and Knowledge Providers, forbidding direct repository discovery or
    orchestration logic within workflows.
  title: Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires consistent interpretation between pattern maturity levels and
    governance decision statuses to prevent premature architectural promotion.
  title: Pattern and Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All new patterns must default to a 'supporting' scope rather than 'core'
    to ensure they are validated through evidence and usage before becoming foundational.
  title: Patterns Must Be Created as Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Forbids the consolidation of patterns that reside in different architectural
    layers to maintain clarity between governance, execution, and reliability concerns.
  title: Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core status requires strong evidence from multiple
    sources or system contexts to ensure architectural stability.
  title: Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source for planning state; all generated
    artifacts must derive their status from this registry.
  title: Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates the use of a specific structured YAML schema for all architectural
    decisions to enable machine processing and UI rendering.
  title: Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must participate in the shared Knowledge Workspace and are prohibited
    from duplicating workspace-level governance structures.
  title: Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Foundational rule defining semantic standards for intent vs. state, decision
    vs. system state, and lifecycle terminology across all artifacts.
  title: Language & Semantics Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns derived from heuristics must include at least one linked signal
    as evidence to ensure traceability to observed behavior.
  title: Heuristic-Derived Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the mandatory precedence order (Global > Project > Prompt) for
    resolving conflicts between rules from different sources.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Enforces human-in-the-loop governance; all system-generated architectural
    proposals must be explicitly approved, rejected, or deferred by an architect.
  title: System Proposes, Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts like AEM and AID summarize authoritative
    sources and must not be used to store primary state.
  title: Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Decisions must be recorded only in ADRs; all other representations
    (metadata, maps) must be derived from these records.
  title: ADR as Single Source of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines mandatory criteria (Recurrence, Impact, Reusability, Stability)
    and evidence requirements for promoting a candidate signal to a pattern.
  title: Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires all architectural decisions to be saved as structured ADR files
    before they can be reflected in system maps or other artifacts.
  title: Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Lifecycle stages of architecture items must be directly mapped from their
    decision status; non-accepted items cannot be marked as DONE.
  title: Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures the Architecture Evolution Map reflects and never contradicts recorded
    Architecture Decision Records.
  title: AEM Consistency with Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Limits core pattern designation to foundational architectural primitives
    rather than context-specific strategies or implementations.
  title: Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
